The `as TestStatusValue` cast is unsafe and will cause a runtime `TypeError` if any story carries one of the three new status values. `statusValueToStoryIdsMap` is only initialized with the five test-status keys (`pending`, `success`, `error`, `warning`, `unknown`), so `statusValueToStoryIdsMap['status-value:new']` evaluates to `undefined`, and calling `.push()` on it throws immediately.

Add a runtime guard before the cast to skip unrecognized values:
```typescript
if (!(status.value in statusValueToStoryIdsMap)) {
  return;
}
statusValueToStoryIdsMap[status.value as TestStatusValue].push(status.storyId);
```
Alternatively, use a type-predicate helper that narrows `StatusValue` to `TestStatusValue`.
